From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:07:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 133/160] rule-set: format text, a list of domains and IP CIDRs
 as plain text

Many sites publish their lists as plain text, a domain or an address a line,
with no rule-set around them. The format text takes such a list as a rule-set,
local or remote: a domain matches itself and its subdomains (domain_suffix),
an address or CIDR matches by destination (ip_cidr); "#" and "//" begin
comments. A domain needs a dot or a leading dot (".ru"): a word alone is text.
A list with no item is an error, so a page served in place of the list (a
block page, a captive portal) does not replace it; the lines left out are
counted in the log of a remote set. The rules are the ones of any rule-set:
only the way the list is written differs (common/ruletext).
